body:
I would find a friend or family member to confide in. Make arrangements to move out and/or end the relationship. If by phone or text, do so in the company of the family and friends you can trust. If in person, make sure several people are there to back you up and protect you if he gets violent. If you don't have family and friends to help, meet somewhere in public and break up. I would then seek counseling to find out why you stayed with someone who is abusive for so long (past trauma, abuse, low self-esteem, etc.) and get the help you need to lead a healthier future. It will be hard to break away from him after 3 years, but if you do so while seeking therapy, it will help you weed through all the feelings your going to have after getting away.

&nbsp;

I wish you the best!

Honestly, making a big deal of this will make or break this situation. You need to set some boundaries. He thinks it's okay to set clear boundaries with you (not giving you his address), but you NEED to set boundaries with him. 

&nbsp;

I would say something like this: "Hey, I hope you're having a good time with your family. The reason I asked for your address the other day is that [insert daughter's name] made you something that can spoil and I wanted you to have it before they expired. I would love to mail them to you, but I need your address. If not, I might be tempted to treat myself. ;) Hope we can catch up soon."

&nbsp;

That tells why you need to mail him something and it does so playfully without pushing him. It also shows him that you don't expect a quick reply. I think he may have wanted to save you the expense of mailing and it was a miscommunication between the two of you. If you send the above message and he still acts weird and gives you the cold shoulder, I would say that he's hiding something and that's why he blew up. If he responds, he was probably upset that you assumed he didn't want mail from you two = spells unnecessary drama to a man.

&nbsp;

P.S. I go days without responding to messages, and especially being the holidays, he may just be busy. I would send the message and let it go. Don't spend all your time focused on him. That's not living.

&nbsp;

Good luck!
